    "block_bbox": [
     173,
     733,
     1047,
     898
    ],
    "block_content": "Following West and Harrison (1997), below we restate the filtering and retrospective recursions needed to sample from $p(\\Theta, \\Sigma \\mid \\eta)$. Note that all densities in this subsection are conditional on the parameters $F_t$, $G_t$, $W_t$, $\\Sigma$, $M_0$ and $C_0$ but that this dependence has been suppressed for notational simplicity. Let us introduce $v_t$ and $\\Xi_t$ as filtering parameters at step $t$. Further, we define $v_0 = v$ and $\\Xi_0 = \\Xi$. As a final piece of notation we introduce $H_t^T$ as a shorthand for the set $\\{\\eta_t^T, \\ldots, \\eta_1^T\\}$"
   },
   {
    "block_id": 14,
    "block_label": "paragraph_title",
    "block_bbox": [
     176,
     922,
     697,
     947
    ],
    "block_content": "B.2.1 Filtering Recursions for MDLM Model"
   },
   {
